WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.737
Exploration is a compulsory human trait.

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:08.708
We're the only animal on the planet driven so deeply by curiosity.

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:12.912
From the surface of the Earth, the ocean floor, to space.

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:16.783
Humans have an insatiable desire for adventure and exploration.

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:21.054
These days we've been turning our eyes to our closest planetary neighbor,

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:21.955
Mars.

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:24.424
Over the last decade,

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:27.327
I've used pro gear to explore some of the furthest reaches of our planet

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:29.429
as a photographer for National Geographic.

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:32.665
Today I'm taking the Oppo Find X3 Pro 

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:34.367
to the Mojave Desert on assignment.

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:38.338
It's the cloest experience you can have to being on Mars.

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:47.247
Photography gives us a chance to experience things we may never get to see.

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:51.384
It's been one of National Geographic's most powerful tools.

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:56.389
To unlock that explorer in all of us.

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:01.995
And show us the sights and colours of incredible places.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.432
It's what's brought me here.

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:07.734
To this cracked, eroded landscape.

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:13.473
Like Mars, it's dry, barren, and incredibly ornate.

00:01:16.276 --> 00:01:19.245
The carved canyons, long shadows, deep craters,

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:24.350
and rich iron oxide soil create a landscape that extends for as far as the eye can see.

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:32.158
Despite being among the driest places on Earth,

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:35.061
the soil is home to extremophiles.

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:38.665
Microscopic organisms that can live in harsh conditions.

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:43.503
Space expedition teams have actually tested Mars rovers here.

00:01:44.237 --> 00:01:48.942
A pretty ideal simulation to prepare them for the rough soil, harsh winds, and steep slopes

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:50.310
that can be found on Mars.

00:01:51.478 --> 00:01:53.847
Exploring anywhere unknown is always challenging.

00:01:54.214 --> 00:01:57.083
And requires perserverance, ingenuity, and dedication.

00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:03.323
When people see my images, my hope is that they will inspire curiosity.

00:02:09.202 --> 00:02:11.971
And to give them the feeling as if they were on Mars.

